  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Dry weather will persist through the weekend.\nWarmer temperatures return for Thursday and Friday with gusty \nwinds on Friday. Seasonable temperatures return for weekend. \n\nMid-level ridging and surface high pressure will dominate\nfavoring mainly dry conditions through the weekend. Clear skies \nwill favor cool nights with likely the coolest night being\ntonight. A cooler airmass in place combined with light winds and \nmainly clear skies will favor efficient radiational cooling\ntonight. Temperatures are likely to fall into the 20s and 30s\nwith the higher terrain, valleys, and usual radiator spots most \nfavored for lows in the mid- upper 20s. Can't rule out a few \nspots in the interior dropping into the low 20s. \n\nDry and seasonably cool temperatures persist into Wednesday. \nTemperatures aloft trend a little warmer as a mid-level ridge \nshifts east which may nudge highs a few degrees warmer than \nTuesday. The warming trend in temperatures continues into late-\nweek resulting in 925mb temperatures warming to +11 to +14C. \nThis will yield high temperatures in the mid-60s on Thursday \nalongside breezy NW winds. Despite the mid-level zonal flow \nFriday (ahead of our next weak wave), the westerly flow will \nsupport efficient mixing in the boundary layer. This will result\nin a gusty/windier day and likely the warmest day of the week \nwith high temperatures in the upper 60s to low 70s. NBM \ncontinues to highlight probabilities 50-75%+ for temperatures \n70F or greater with the highest probabilities for the valleys \nand I-95 metros. This is reasonable given the added factor of \nthe warming downslope flow. A mild late-October day is looking \nlikely. \n\nAnother moisture-starved shortwave and cold front moves\novernight Friday. This will shift temperatures back into the\nlower 60s this weekend, which is seasonable for late October.\n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Transition to a more unsettled weather pattern by\nearly next week bringing periodic chances for rain. Confidence \nin specific timing remains low. \n\nLooking ahead to next week, ensemble guidance shows agreement \nwith a transition to a unsettled weather pattern. This will\nfeature series of shortwave troughs bringing periodic chances \nfor rain. However, there is still a fair amount of spread \nacross guidance in the details of the pattern including details\nof the pattern which has reduced confidence in the timing of\nrain chances through the week.",
